      "problem": "Simplify the polynomial $x^3+x-2x^2-3x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, $x$ and $-3x$ are like terms, so we group them, and then we add or subtract the coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+x-2{x}^{2}-3x & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+x-3x-2{x}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+(x-3x)-2{x}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+(1-3)x-2{x}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-2x-2{x}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
